    "body": "Every SGLang explainer video now ends with a fixed **关注 SGLang** strip: GitHub `github.com/sgl-project/sglang` · 博客 `sglang.io/blog` · 文档 `docs.sglang.io`.\n\n![follow strip](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BBuf/AI-Infra-Auto-Driven-SKILLS/sglang-explainer-video-follow-strip/skills/sglang-explainer-video/assets/brand/follow-strip-example.png)\n\n## Changes\n- `assets/brand/follow-strip.html` holds the strip's CSS and markup. The last-frame worker pastes it verbatim.\n  - Placement: y 792–872, just above the caption band.\n  - It is on screen only and is not narrated.\n- `references/house-style.md` adds a new section, §Follow strip. `SKILL.md` step 3 and `references/worker-dispatch.md` were also updated, so the storyboard and the last-frame worker both reserve space for the strip (frame content ends above y≈770).\n- `scripts/check_frames.mjs` now fails the last frame if the strip is missing or any of its three URLs is missing.\n- Plugin version 0.9.3 → 0.9.4.\n\n## Test\nOn a copy of the Step 5 Preview project, the strip was pasted into the last frame. Results:\n- `check_frames` → OK.\n- `subset_fonts` covered the new CJK text.\n- `hf lint` → 0 errors.\n- `hf snapshot` at the final second shows the strip (the image above).\n\nOn the unmodified project, `check_frames` reports `FAIL 17-summary.html — last frame lacks the SGLang follow strip`, as expected.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
